      "hints": [
        "Multiply across by $\\cos\\theta$ to form $2\\cos^2\\theta - 7\\cos\\theta + 3 = 0$.",
        "Factorise $(2\\cos\\theta - 1)(\\cos\\theta - 3) = 0$.",
        "Solve $\\cos\\theta = \\frac{1}{2}$ for $\\theta$ in the interval $-90^\\circ < \\theta < 90^\\circ$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Clear the fraction by multiplying both sides by $\\cos\\theta$:\n$$2\\cos\\theta = 7 - \\frac{3}{\\cos\\theta} \\implies 2\\cos^2\\theta - 7\\cos\\theta + 3 = 0$$",
        "Factorise the quadratic in $\\cos\\theta$:\n$$(2\\cos\\theta - 1)(\\cos\\theta - 3) = 0$$",
        "Solve for $\\cos\\theta$ (rejecting $\\cos\\theta = 3$ since $|\\cos\\theta| \\le 1$):\n$$\\cos\\theta = \\frac{1}{2}$$",
        "Find both solutions in the open domain $-90^\\circ < \\theta < 90^\\circ$:\n$$\\theta = -60^\\circ \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\theta = 60^\\circ$$"
      ],
